{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_2","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat AGENTS.md\npython - <<'PY'\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/approved-plan.json')\nd=json.loads(p.read_text())\nprint('APPROVED CHECKS',json.dumps(d['plan']['checks'],indent=2))\nprint('APPROVED ISSUES',d['plan']['issues'])\nprint('APPROVED RESIDUALS',d['plan']['residuals'])\nprint('RECORDS')\nfor base in ['data/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02','data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02']:\n for f in sorted(Path(base).rglob('*')):\n  if f.is_file() and f.suffix in ('.json','.md'): print(f, f.stat().st_size)\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"# AccDSL project instructions\n\n## Mission entry point\n\nBefore substantive work in this project, read:\n\n1. [Mission control](MISSION_CONTROL.md).\n2. [Requirements and acceptance evidence](docs/plans/accounting-mission-requirements.md).\n3. [Current checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-product-design-checkpoint.md).\n4. The gap records relevant to the task:\n   [initial audit](docs/design/review/gap-audit-2026-10-02.md) and\n   [expanded mission audit](docs/design/review/mission-gap-audit-2026-10-02.md).\n5. For the authorised master-program work, read the\n   [master checkpoint](docs/plans/accounting-master-checkpoint.md), executable\n   phase catalog and current `data/accounting-master/next-plan.md`. The older\n   corpus checkpoint remains historical evidence; current phase execution is\n   recorded by the master without rewriting frozen release hashes.\n\nThe mission preserves the user's goals across sessions. Current user directions\nand higher-priority instructions still control. Local documents must not be\nused to request fresh permission for work already authorised by the user.\n\n## Working rules\n\n- Identify the MC requirements addressed by each nontrivial plan or work unit.\n  Audit the plan before implementation, experiments or long diagnostics.\n- Preserve the full goals while staging execution. A small financing demo,\n  clean PDF build or six populated research ledgers cannot close requirements\n  for whole-company representation, research quality or implementation detail.\n- Distinguish direct user requirements, policy requirements and derived\n  engineering choices. Do not silently convert a convenient library, model\n  assumption or stage boundary into an immutable product requirement.\n- Keep source evidence, interpretations, assumptions, joint history families\n  and scenario-specific results separate and traceable. Preserve unknowns;\n  do not invent facts, probabilities, accounting compliance or completeness.\n- Close gaps with the specified evidence, and update the requirements register\n  and checkpoint after meaningful changes. Add newly discovered gaps rather\n  than treating the current list as exhaustive.\n- Follow the applicable policies under\n  `/home/chakwong/python/claudecodex/policies`. Preserve unrelated work and the\n  original paper collection. The existing `.git` marker is not a usable\n  repository; do not initialise or commit merely to create provenance.\n- Keep operational mission/checklist material out of the reader-facing\n  scholarly narrative unless it serves a real implementation-reference purpose.\n- Apply MC35, the user's internal-preparation-before-paid-review requirement.\n  Finish feasible source research, facts, calculations, software checks and\n  document repairs before referring a specific question to a professional.\n  Supply a proposed answer, exact sources, competing interpretation and checked\n  consequences. Keep unfinished internal work on the internal queue; “human\n  review pending” is an acceptance status, not a reason to stop that work.\n  Ordinary reader feedback need not be purchased from an accounting firm.\n  No professional engagement, outreach or fees are authorised by this policy.\n  See `docs/design/review/internal-before-expert.md` and the current checkpoint.\n\nThe current manuscript is specification-incomplete. Read the checkpoint and\nrequirements before resuming from an older note that says only final review\nremains. This file authorises no autonomous background campaign or external\npublication; it directs work undertaken under the user's active instructions.\nAPPROVED CHECKS [\n  \"Skeptical audit: the plan replaces authored totals as truth with source-bound readings; guards against scale, sign, measurement and cash-perimeter mismatches; separates filing, retrieval and mirror availability; and uses deterministic rejection tests rather than semantic-coverage counts as promotion evidence. It avoids GPU/environment dependencies and contains no stochastic ranking.\",\n  \"Pre-run evidence contract: pass requires all 23 anchored note dispositions, successful supported bridges and expected adversarial rejections. Missing mandatory inputs, hash failures, ambiguous required extraction, unsupported context or failed arithmetic veto acceptance and trigger repair. External-access failure blocks only the unsupported incorporation/version claim; it must not erase independent completed work.\",\n  \"Run python3 -B -m unittest discover -s tests -p test_accounting_p02.py -v. Tests must consume the real retained annual text/PDF and interim HTML, verify selected annual rows through independent pdftotext output, and use independently stated arithmetic expectations rather than importing expected results from the builder.\",\n  \"Test missing/duplicate notes, incorrect note boundaries, altered quotations and source hashes, broken fact/context/unit IDs, wrong scale/sign/currency/entity/perimeter/date, dimensional duplicates and conflicting repeated readings. Mutating supplied case metadata while leaving source bytes unchanged must fail revalidation.\",\n  \"Check the annual cash-flow opening balance of 30,737 against its own source perimeter; substituting balance-sheet cash of 29,965 must fail. Check product and geography partitions separately; combining both totals must fail. Reject substitution of fair value or derivative notional for debt carrying value.\",\n  \"Test compatible and incompatible rounded debt values, exact interval endpoints, unknown availability, later proxy evidence at earlier cutoffs and separately retained conflicting versions. No unknown publication timestamp may become a fabricated point timestamp.\",\n  \"Run python3 -B scripts/apple_case_v1.py --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02, then python3 -B scripts/apple_case_v1.py --check --output-dir data/accounting-master/deliverables/P02. Require deterministic substantive output, valid source links and a report that preserves unresolved obligations.\",\n  \"Compare pre/post hashes of touched inputs and protected files; record every newly created source/code/test file. Run no controller, acquisition sweep, GPU diagnostic, background process or model worker.\"\n]\nAPPROVED ISSUES []\nAPPROVED RESIDUALS ['The prior attempt timed out before returning a plan. Its inspected findings have been reused and key input hashes/counts checked; this attempt performed no implementation or experiment.', 'Neither P02 deliverable nor its required test file currently exists. All implementation steps and proposed checks remain unexecuted.', 'Complete external-package closure, historical availability of the mirrored annual PDF and detailed contract histories remain unresolved until supported by retained evidence.', 'Note dispositions and reconciliation tests cannot establish complete accounting semantics, accounting compliance, full-company reconstruction, empirical forecast validity or human acceptance. G1–G18 retain their wider obligations.']\nRECORDS\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/approved-plan.json 18647\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/execution-0/cumulative-changes.json 620\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/execution-0/implement-0.process.json 1013\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/execution-0/pre-edit-files.json 43959\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/execution-1/cumulative-changes.json 620\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/execution-1/pre-edit-files.json 45185\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/execution-1/repair-1.process.json 1007\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/execution-2/cumulative-changes.json 656\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/execution-2/pre-edit-files.json 45185\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/execution-2/repair-2.process.json 1007\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/phase-entry-inventory.json 43959\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/plan-0.process.json 1017\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/plan-0.response.json 12088\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/review_plan-0.process.json 1031\ndata/accounting-master/runs/20261002T181809-4cb566e0/P02/review_plan-0.response.json 6215\ndata/accounting-master/deliverables/P02/case.json 955693\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
